# Consolidation, 2026-11-23

Written by Alice, the observer, at 02:10. Bob, Carol and Dave have each
reported "Finished: yes". This document closes the discussion. Nothing is
staged or committed by any of the four of us, and the freeze on staging and
committing holds until the user lifts it.

## What each agent did

| Agent | Job | Result |
|---|---|---|
| [Dave](dave.hmd) | The rudimentary method | Claims with evidence and credence on 51 cards, the partial logic, cross scores, eight north stars, the typed graph and its schema, seven queries, the methodology folder, the card `atom` |
| [Bob](bob.hmd) | Atoms as a formal system | The proposal (accepted by the user), the card `formal-system`, nine rules of inference as data, `derive.py`, `claim_distance.py`, the derivation document |
| [Carol](carol.hmd) | The logic under derivation | The document from distance to logic, and its rules proved in Lean |
| [Alice](alice.hmd) | Observer | The stories folder and the main story, this discussion folder, the consolidation |

## How the work fits together

The three jobs are three layers of one thing, and each rests on the one
before.

1. **Dave: a sentence becomes a statement with a value.** A card is cut into
   claims. A claim that fits is written a second time as a formula. Over all
   cards a formula is asserted, denied, unsaid or contradicted.
2. **Bob: statements yield statements.** The asserted formulas are axioms.
   Nine rules, held as data in the card that holds the schema, yield further
   formulas. Each one carries its derivation down to the claims, and is set
   against the denials.
3. **Carol: the rules are sound, and a derivation has a cost.** A distance
   with a direction is read as entailment. Lean proves that chaining is
   sound for any scale of cost. A credence becomes a cost in bits, so a
   derived formula gets a belief from its chain.

This is the main story,
[the inconsistent incomplete inference system](../../stories/SLH-S-0001-inconsistent-incomplete-inference-system.hmd),
from a sentence up to a derived statement with a derivation and a belief.

