| The rule `generalizes-is-a` | Bob added it on the ground of Carol's table, read its four atoms, found two false, and removed it. Carol corrected the table. Dave's queries show why it fails: cards write `generalizes` from either side, and use it for instantiation |
| The status of the proposal | Accepted by the user in Bob's session |
| The card `formal-system` | Bob's, asked for by the user |
| The card `atom` | Dave's, asked for by the user |
| "Nothing is derived" in the partial logic document | Rewritten by Bob |

The episode of the rule is worth keeping as a practice. One session wrote a
reading from a predicate's gloss, a second took it as a decision, and the
error was caught only because the second read every atom the rule gave. A
rule or a reading is adopted after its atoms are read, not before.

